{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20432",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 4.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.13,
      "end_seconds": 10.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "So, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.66,
      "end_seconds": 14.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.15,
      "end_seconds": 18.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.29,
      "end_seconds": 27.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Honestly, it's a cut on my finger, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.51,
      "end_seconds": 30.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Okay, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.0,
      "end_seconds": 41.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "I've had it for ten days. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.19,
      "end_seconds": 45.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.58,
      "end_seconds": 51.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "It usually comes with bleeding. And difficulty bending the finger, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.67,
      "end_seconds": 55.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.69,
      "end_seconds": 75.33,
      "duration_seconds": 17.64,
      "text": "I'd give it a three, out of ten. The bleeding? That's been since last weekend. I've also had pain in the finger. As for pain in the finger, I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.91,
      "end_seconds": 83.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Have you had a cut on your finger before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.44,
      "end_seconds": 89.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last year. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.25,
      "end_seconds": 94.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Any fever, weakness of the hand or bite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.97,
      "end_seconds": 98.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.7,
      "end_seconds": 104.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "A few quick ones: redness spreading or dirt in the wound?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.1,
      "end_seconds": 107.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.68,
      "end_seconds": 113.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.45,
      "end_seconds": 116.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.44,
      "end_seconds": 123.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.06,
      "end_seconds": 135.18,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Erm, I had a reaction to erythromycin when I was younger, bad stomach cramps, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.01,
      "end_seconds": 140.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Right, anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.65,
      "end_seconds": 147.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Yes, I had a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.59,
      "end_seconds": 166.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.34,
      "end_seconds": 178.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "It's alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week. I'm on naproxen, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.74,
      "end_seconds": 181.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.98,
      "end_seconds": 194.66,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "250 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. I'm on febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 195.98,
      "end_seconds": 201.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "That's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure he takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.17,
      "end_seconds": 206.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.99,
      "end_seconds": 211.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I have thin bones, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.48,
      "end_seconds": 214.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.7,
      "end_seconds": 225.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.78,
      "end_seconds": 228.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.12,
      "end_seconds": 232.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I have gout, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.46,
      "end_seconds": 237.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Okay, I can see gout in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.34,
      "end_seconds": 253.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.83,
      "end_seconds": 268.65,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I've never touched a cigarette. I walk the dog every morning. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.12,
      "end_seconds": 273.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.12,
      "end_seconds": 280.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Oh, my father has Parkinson's disease. My father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.32,
      "end_seconds": 284.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.63,
      "end_seconds": 295.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.47,
      "end_seconds": 327.76,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "Okay: weight 93 kilos, BP is 114 over 81, height 150 centimetres. And BMI works out to 41.3, saturation 99 percent, temperature is 36.6 degrees, heart rate 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.75,
      "end_seconds": 331.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.63,
      "end_seconds": 333.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.8,
      "end_seconds": 335.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.42,
      "end_seconds": 361.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.98,
      "end_seconds": 366.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.96,
      "end_seconds": 402.29,
      "duration_seconds": 20.33,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury. An infected wound is still possible. I'm going to order an X-ray of the finger, for laceration. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.34,
      "end_seconds": 405.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.24,
      "end_seconds": 434.55,
      "duration_seconds": 28.31,
      "text": "The treatment will be tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day. That should help with tetanus prevention. Keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. If the wound becomes red, hot or swollen, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.39,
      "end_seconds": 438.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Yes, I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.39,
      "end_seconds": 446.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Let's plan a check in five days. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.42,
      "end_seconds": 448.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}